-- gap[104] · a branch that MUTATES STATE and emits, so a lost body is visible
-- as a wrong NUMBER and not only as a missing line.
--
-- Every other fixture here would also pass if the branch ran and the prints
-- were merely reordered. This one cannot: `total` reads 3, then 7, then 7 after
-- the `if`, so the arithmetic pins the order and the count of executions. A
-- body executed twice reads 3|7|10|14|14, a body skipped reads 0, and a body
-- whose tail statement is dropped reads 3|3 — three distinct wrong answers,
-- none of which is the expected one.
--
-- `total` is a LOCAL, deliberately. A file-scope global would have been the more
-- natural spelling and it is currently miscompiled by the direct backend
-- independently of anything to do with branches (`total += k` inside a function
-- does not reach the global; measured direct=5 against C=8 on a three-line
-- program with no `if` in it). Using one here would make this row red for a
-- reason it does not test. That defect is filed separately.

main = (): i64
    total: i64 = 0
    if 42 > 10
        total += 3
        print(total)
        total += 4
        print(total)
    print(total)
    0
